# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build context filter for the ROOT Dockerfile (the IRIS FastAPI backend).
#
# Three reasons anything appears here: it is a SECRET, it is multi-hundred-MB
# RUNTIME STATE that belongs in a volume, or it is a HOST-ONLY artifact that
# cannot work inside Linux. Without this file the context is >1 GB and the image
# would carry every API key in the project.
#
# DO NOT add: *.py, prompts/, skills/, IRIS.md, agent.md, security.md,
# requirements.docker.txt — the Dockerfile COPYs all of them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds ~48 keys (the per-subagent model API keys, SLACK_BOT_TOKEN,
# ATTIO_ACCESS_TOKEN, JIRA_API_TOKEN, RESEND_API_KEY, GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD,
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, BACKEND_JWT_SECRET, GOOGLE_OAUTH_*,
# TAVILY_API_KEY, LANGCHAIN_API_KEY). A COPY bakes them into a layer that
# survives any later delete. They arrive at RUN time via compose `env_file:`.
.env
.env.*
# google_auth.py:80 caches the Google OAuth token here (GOOGLE_TOKEN_FILE);
# google_token.disconnected is the current sentinel. Bearer credentials — never
# in an image layer.
google_token.*

# ── Host-only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Windows CPython 3.14 venv: ~GB of .pyd/.exe that cannot execute on Linux, and
# the wrong interpreter version besides. The image installs from
# requirements.docker.txt instead.
project_venv/

# ── Runtime state (belongs in a volume, not a layer) ─────────────────────────
# iris_checkpoints.sqlite is ~150 MB on its own, and copying a live SQLite file
# alongside its -wal/-shm siblings yields a torn snapshot, not a usable DB.
iris_checkpoints.sqlite
iris_checkpoints.sqlite-*
iris_store.sqlite
iris_store.sqlite-*
# ~19 MB of LangGraph Studio pickles from `langgraph dev` — unrelated to the
# uvicorn entry point.
.langgraph_api/
logs/
# Recreated by the Dockerfile / at import: web_search.py:178 mkdirs tmp/,
# agent_memory.py:70 mkdirs workspace/. tmp/ also holds dev probe scripts and
# uvicorn logs; workspace/ holds prior uploads.
tmp/
workspace/
home/

# ── Dev-only trees ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
scratch/
.claude/
.git
.gitignore

# ── The sibling UI image's inputs and outputs ───────────────────────────────
# The backend never reads any of it; ui/node_modules is the single largest
# directory in the repo. (docker-compose.yml builds the UI with `context: ./ui`,
# where ui/.dockerignore applies — these entries only shrink the BACKEND context.)
ui/node_modules/
ui/.next/
ui/out/
ui/__pycache__/
ui/.env
ui/.env.*
ui/*.log

# ── Python bytecode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ── Docs and one-off reports that no module loads ───────────────────────────
# NOTE the deliberate omissions: IRIS.md, agent.md and security.md are NOT
# excluded — IRIS.py:189 loads them as the agent's memory sources.
API_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md
SECURITY_REVIEW.md
IRIS_task_execution_log.md
DOCKER.md
docker-compose.yml
*_summary.md
*_draft.md
prompt injection.md
# The unpinned/Windows-only dependency dump; requirements.docker.txt replaces it
# and is intentionally still included.
requirements.txt
company_announcements_research.txt
langgraph.json
